  "conclusions": [
    "Per-frame WeakRef dereference alone was insufficient to explain retention: a separate Chromium blank-page control collected a weak-only object during active RAF polling on the first forced GC.",
    "Original inventory control retained both cycle0 and cycle1 Actors after stopping polling and three later-task GCs.",
    "Only moving inventory dispose-listener creation to an external factory allowed historical cycle0 Actor collection by released1, while weak polling remained active. It stayed collected through final and four later-task GCs. Latest cycle1 remained retained.",
    "Both controls released the Crab primitive mesh, with one geometry and one material disposal per activation. Actor retention and mesh retirement are separate observations.",
    "The observer factory was changed only in a scratch diagnostic module. Canonical no-inventory reruns are needed for final CPU/heap/Actor claims; original inventory Actor-retention flags must not be reported as application leaks."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Chromium software WebGL at the recorded small mobile viewport; no retail hardware, iPad hardware, WebKit or driver residency claim.",
    "Two short gameplay cycles establish the diagnostic contrast and the numeric pooled-owner observation; no unbounded Actor-growth conclusion.",
    "One late ScreenFX pointer and the InkFlight pool independently retain the latest Actor. Fixing only one does not imply complete latest-Actor collection.",
    "The151MiB heap snapshot is local diagnostic evidence only and must not be committed. No raw model/image data was produced by this audit."
  ],
